cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Studium in your research, please cite it using these metadata."
title: Studium
abstract: >-
  Studium turns sources into adaptive lessons grounded in a typed Learning Workflow Graph,
  playable in VS Code or through any MCP harness, with assessment that records who wrote
  the answer key and whether a judge assessed the answer, spaced review and local-first
  learner data.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Nothias
    given-names: Louis-Félix
    affiliation: "Institut de Chimie de Nice (ICN, UMR 7272), Université Côte d'Azur, CNRS"
  - name: HolobiomicsLab
version: 0.3.0
date-released: 2026-11-09
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/HolobiomicsLab/studium"
keywords:
  - adaptive learning
  - education
  - learning workflow graph
  - spaced repetition
  - model context protocol
  - provenance
